                        <field name="dc_description">This sidecar from 1908 was built for the then Society for High and Underground Railways in Berlin. Between 1902 and 1926, 254 side-cars of this type were procured. It is the oldest surviving subway car in Berlin and was in operation at BVG (-W) until 1966. It still appears today.<br/>
The cart box is made of wood and is faithfully preserved. The brake system is an original, electrically controlled two-chamber compressed air brake that acts on the wheels via wooden blocks.<br/>
<br/>
Schipporeit, Reiner; Reinhard Demps. Historical vehicles in Berlin: buses, trams, subway, subway. Berlin: Museum of Transport and Technology, 1991.  (Deutsches Technikmuseum) </field>
